# Composite Kbuild for r8125_rust.ko (Rust + C-shim OOT module).
#
# Crate root: r8125_rust.rs (Rust). C bridge: netdev_bridge.c (per plan §5.2
# / §6.3, providing net_device / NAPI / sk_buff glue that has no stable
# kernel-Rust API yet). Both objects link into a single r8125_rust.ko.
#
# Pattern mirrors samples/rust/rust_print (rust_print_main.rs +
# rust_print_events.c → rust_print.ko). C and Rust components live in the
# same M= directory because kbuild's composite-object syntax requires it.
obj-m += r8125_rust.o

# Note: the Rust crate root is r8125_rust_main.rs, NOT r8125_rust.rs.
# Naming the composite (r8125_rust.o) the same as the Rust component
# triggers a kbuild circular-dep warning and silently drops the Rust .o
# from the final link. Same trick samples/rust/rust_print uses.
r8125_rust-y := r8125_rust_main.o netdev_bridge.o netdev_bridge_phy.o \
                netdev_bridge_offload.o netdev_bridge_ethtool.o
